ROOT CAUSE (static trace, confirms live observation):
Two DIFFERENT call sites both fire getProfile() on every successful login, and NEITHER
was touched by this ticket's diff (git diff feat/userapp-reskin2...HEAD --stat shows only
home_screen.dart + splash_screen.dart touched in both apps -- auth_service.dart and
sign_in_screen.dart are untouched):
  1. VendorApp/lib/features/auth/domain/services/auth_service.dart:128 (manageLogin(),
     non-subscribed branch) -- fire-and-forget `Get.find<ProfileController>().getProfile();`
     (not awaited).
  2. VendorApp/lib/features/auth/screens/sign_in_screen.dart:241 -- `await
     Get.find<ProfileController>().getProfile();` in the post-login `.then()` callback.
The ticket's own grooming text explicitly named site #1 (auth_service.dart:127-128,
"corrected location") as IN SCOPE for the consolidation ("Scope (in): ... the VendorApp
login-flow fire-and-forget call (`auth_service.dart:127`, corrected location)"), but the
shipped diff never touches this file. home_screen.dart's new `profileModel == null` guard
only prevents the THIRD (home-screen) fetch that the original 3x audit finding measured;
it does not address the pre-existing duplication between call sites #1 and #2, which still
both fire concurrently on every login (cold or warm).

AC2 requires "login issues at most 1" -- 2 is observed. This is a breaks_ac defect.
